    "['track [parameter1] interface [parameter2] line-protocol', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set chassis network-services enhanced-ip', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set chassis network-services enhanced-ip', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `track` command:\\n\\n##\\nset chassis network-services enhanced-ip\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 gigether-options redundant-parent reth0\\nset interfaces reth0 redundant-ether-options redundancy-group 2\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles interface tracking differently than Cisco. The above translation creates a redundancy group (similar to Cisco's tracking) for interface ge-1/0/1. \\n\\nIf you specifically need the exact tracking functionality for OSPF/VRRP purposes, an alternative would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track-interface ge-1/0/1\\n##\\n\\nFor exact line-protocol tracking equivalence in Junos, you would typically configure it as part of the interface monitoring or under protocols (like OSPF/VRRP) rather than as a standalone tracking command.\", 'trans_template': 'set chassis network-services enhanced-ip'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 gigether-options redundant-parent reth0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 gigether-options redundant-parent reth0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `track` command:\\n\\n##\\nset chassis network-services enhanced-ip\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 gigether-options redundant-parent reth0\\nset interfaces reth0 redundant-ether-options redundancy-group 2\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles interface tracking differently than Cisco. The above translation creates a redundancy group (similar to Cisco's tracking) for interface ge-1/0/1. \\n\\nIf you specifically need the exact tracking functionality for OSPF/VRRP purposes, an alternative would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track-interface ge-1/0/1\\n##\\n\\nFor exact line-protocol tracking equivalence in Junos, you would typically configure it as part of the interface monitoring or under protocols (like OSPF/VRRP) rather than as a standalone tracking command.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 gigether-options redundant-parent reth0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces reth0 redundant-ether-options redundancy-group 2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces reth0 redundant-ether-options redundancy-group 2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `track` command:\\n\\n##\\nset chassis network-services enhanced-ip\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 gigether-options redundant-parent reth0\\nset interfaces reth0 redundant-ether-options redundancy-group 2\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles interface tracking differently than Cisco. The above translation creates a redundancy group (similar to Cisco's tracking) for interface ge-1/0/1. \\n\\nIf you specifically need the exact tracking functionality for OSPF/VRRP purposes, an alternative would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track-interface ge-1/0/1\\n##\\n\\nFor exact line-protocol tracking equivalence in Junos, you would typically configure it as part of the interface monitoring or under protocols (like OSPF/VRRP) rather than as a standalone tracking command.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces reth0 redundant-ether-options redundancy-group 2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track-interface ge-1/0/1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/1 unit 0 family inet address 10.0.0.1/24 vrrp-group 10 track-interface ge-1/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `track` command:\\n\\n##\\nset chassis network-services enhanced-ip\\nset interfaces ge-1/0